  "mathematical_reason": "The actual normalized softmax masses and genuine partition lower bound derive critical-action probability<=exp((u1-v1)/alpha+u2-p*u3/alpha). For alpha>0,u3>0,delta>0 the bound is<=delta exactly when p>=gap/u3+(u2-log(delta))*alpha/u3. At the illustrative constants the exact penalties are11+log10 and14+4log10; actual rational logarithm enclosures prove the two-decimal displays13.30 and23.21, and the increments0.5log10 and2log10 round to1.15 and4.61. The first display13.30 is below the true threshold, so presenting the exact symbolic threshold before its approximate decimal avoids asserting that rounded number itself guarantees safety. The original4.605 is only an approximation of2log10. The actual sufficient threshold grows affinely with alpha; a conservative sufficient bound growing does not itself imply actual unsafety. The revised final phrase attributes fixed-penalty degradation to the primary cliff-world experiment, which Section6.1.2 and Fig3 directly report, and accurately retains the paper recommendation to scale penalty with temperature. All five changes are narrow numerical/explanatory precision corrections; the entire current/proposed Exercise7.6 and node1174 were read, but this review does not approve whole24 or the whole exercise.",
